WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.289
Think of a lake. The water line is the top edge and the curved bed is the bottom edge. The depth at any point is top minus bottom. Adding the depths gives the area.

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:26.631
The same works for two graphs. The area between them is the integral of top minus bottom. Here the line y equals x is above the curve y equals x squared, from nought to one.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:35.782
The limits are where the graphs meet. There the two y values are equal, so set the two equations equal and solve.

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:49.284
Which graph is on top? Test one x value between the limits. At x equals a half, the line gives a half and the curve a quarter. So the line is on top.

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:58.338
These questions ask for the area of the finite region bounded by a curve and a line, or two curves. Finite means enclosed all the way round.

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:10.748
Step one: solve the two equations together, to get the limits. Step two: test a value between the limits to see which graph is on top.

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:21.417
Step three: simplify top minus bottom, then integrate. Step four: substitute the limits, keeping the answer exact if asked.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:27.805
The trap is subtracting the wrong way round. Bottom minus top gives a negative area.

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:46.747
November twenty twenty three. The curve S is y equals x squared over two, minus two x, minus six. The line l is two y plus x plus eight equals nought. Find the exact area bounded by S and l. Seven marks.

00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:55.693
Here is the picture. The line l cuts the parabola S at P, and at one more point. The shaded region lies between them.

00:01:56.280 --> 00:02:07.172
Step one: the limits. Set l equal to S. That gives x squared minus three x minus four equals nought, so x is minus one or four.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:20.201
Step two: test x equals nought. The line gives minus four, S gives minus six, so l is on top. Integrate l minus S. The minus applies to every term of S.

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:33.386
Step three: integrate and put in the limits. At four we get twenty eight thirds. At minus one we get minus thirteen twelfths. The difference is one hundred and twenty five twelfths.

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:40.861
So the exact area is one hundred and twenty five over twelve. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:55.305
A common mistake is dropping a minus sign. When you subtract S, the minus applies to every term inside the bracket. So minus minus two x becomes plus two x.

00:02:56.440 --> 00:03:16.209
Now you try, from November twenty twenty. C is y equals x squared, minus nine x, plus fourteen. The line l is y equals x plus five. Find the exact area of the finite region bounded by C and l. Write your answer, then choose Continue to Answer.

00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:26.897
Set the equations equal: x squared minus ten x plus nine is nought, so x is one or nine. The line is on top between them.

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:39.990
Line minus curve is minus x squared plus ten x minus nine. Integrating gives eighty one at nine, and minus thirteen thirds at one. The area is two hundred and fifty six thirds.

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:49.067
The common wrong answer subtracts the wrong way round. That gives minus two fifty six thirds. An area cannot be negative.

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:56.716
Remember: solve together, test for the top graph, integrate top minus bottom, then use the limits.
